[NOT RUN] DAY-02 (restart persistence)
Reason: needs two separate terminal invocations sharing the same broker-day
global-variable state; not attempted this session given the destructive-test
authorization boundary was the priority.

[NOT RUN] LOSS-04 (opt-in liquidation) / EMR-04 (emergency opt-in liquidation) /
CLOSE-01..04 (multi-symbol filling, retry, retry ceiling, retry restart)
Reason: destructive by design (ClosePositionsOnEmergencyStop /
ClosePositionsOnDailyLossBreach = true actually closes positions). Left for
explicit authorization before running, per the plan's default-OFF posture on
destructive actions.

[NOT RUN] TRADE-04 (HistorySelect failure) / RISK-05 (OrderCalcProfit failure) /
PERSIST-01..03 (SafeGlobalSet / lock-write / retry-write failures)
Reason: these require injecting a terminal-API failure (a broken HistorySelect,
OrderCalcProfit, or GlobalVariableSet call) that a real MT5 terminal does not
expose a way to force; TEST_PLAN.md already scopes these as needing "a
controlled environment" beyond a live/demo terminal.

